-symbol` entry stops reporting a missing bead.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Publish sase-core 0.11.3 and raise the declared minimum[/bold #D7AFFF]       [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]corefloor[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]corefloor: land the open sase-core release so the five [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`plan_reference_*` bindings reach PyPI, then raise sase's declared [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`sase-core-rs` floor and its tracking test to the published version.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Give the mark_all_read anchor a documented variance factor[/bold #D7AFFF]    [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]perffloor[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]perffloor: add a per-anchor `rust_slowdown_factor` override with a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]written rationale for the one write-heavy notification anchor whose [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]ceiling has no slack, matching the mechanism already used for its two [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]sibling anchors.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Confirm master is green and triage residual test flakes[/bold #D7AFFF]       [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]verify[dim] · [dim][/dim]after beadstore, corefloor, perffloor[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]verify: confirm a full CI run passes with all three fixes present, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]determine whether the two `test (3.14)` failures seen once on master are[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]flakes or real defects.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-a0","llm_provider":"codex","model":"gpt-5.6-sol","phase_bead_id":"sase-a0.1","reasoning_effort":"high","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-39